{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"aa03f46c-0c0f-40f4-b7eb-6f06fcd5cf1e","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Both issues have been investigated and fixed:\n\n1. **`invertAffine()` in [`src/core/3d/math.ts`](file:///Users/pranav/Project%20Folder/WebAPPBuilder/src/core/3d/math.ts#L186-L235)**\n   - **What was wrong:** The upper 3x3 block inversion had rows and columns transposed in its cofactor assignment (`res[1]` held $C_{10}$ instead of $C_{01}$), diverging from general `invert()` when scaling was non-uniform.\n   - **What was changed:** Recomputed the 3x3 inverse matrix via adjugate $B_{i,j} = C_{j,i}/\\det$ in column-major order and translation as $-A^{-1} t$, restoring exact numerical parity between `invertAffine()` and `invert()`.\n\n2. **`setOriginToCenterOfMass` test cube in [`src/core/3d/__tests__/apply.test.ts`](file:///Users/pranav/Project%20Folder/WebAPPBuilder/src/core/3d/__tests__/apply.test.ts#L87-L89)**\n   - **What was wrong:** The signed-tetrahedra math in `apply.ts` was mathematically correct, but `createSampleCubeMesh()` in the unit test defined the Top (+Y) face indices as `3, 2, 6, 3, 6, 7` (clockwise inward normal $[0, -4, 0]$), causing negative volume cancellation against outward-facing faces.\n   - **What was changed:** Corrected Top face winding to counter-clockwise (`3, 6, 2, 3, 7, 6`, outward normal $[0, +4, 0]$). The 12 triangles across all 6 faces now consistently integrate to volume +8, centering the offset cube at $[5, -3, 2]$ and satisfying `positions[0] === -1` and `positions[18] === +1`.\n\nDetailed notes and handoff:\n- Running notes: [`DOCS/3D/tasks/3D-008.notes.md`](file:///Users/pranav/Project%20Folder/WebAPPBuilder/DOCS/3D/tasks/3D-008.notes.md)\n- Fix handoff: [`DOCS/3D/tasks/3D-008.fix1.handoff.md`](file:///Users/pranav/Project%20Folder/WebAPPBuilder/DOCS/3D/tasks/3D-008.fix1.handoff.md)\n","duration_seconds":1594.352234,"num_turns":2,"usage":{"input_tokens":454956,"output_tokens":128167,"thinking_tokens":84342,"cache_